url: "https://raspberry-kim.github.io/donghyun-lab12/"
abstract: >-
  Donghyunsim is a browser-based, noncommercial city-building toy that
  follows only the skeleton of SimCity DS (Nintendo DS, 2007; developed by
  AKI Corporation and EA Japan, published by Electronic Arts), itself based
  on SimCity 3000. On a 40x40 plain crossed by a river, expandable to 60x60, the player
  lays roads and power lines, places 3x3 residential, commercial and
  industrial zones, and builds a power plant, police and fire stations and
  parks. Zones that are both powered and reached by a road grow through five
  levels according to demand, land value, pollution and crime; taxes arrive
  and upkeep is paid every month, and the city title changes with
  population. Optional events (festival, donation, tourists, tree planting)
  and disasters (fire, flood, a giant monster) occur at random. The only
  settings, the starting funds option (0-3) and the event and disaster
  switches (0/1), are chosen through a program written in the esoteric
  programming language Donghyun-lang. Input is mouse and touch only, with
  fullscreen; keyboard and gamepad are intentionally unsupported. The city
  is saved in the browser and can be exported to and imported from a
  .dhsave file. All 89 tiles and icons are drawn anew by tools/tiles.py and
  tools/architecture.py; version 0.11 redraws all 30 zone stages and 18 facilities.
  The news faces are the 16x16 faces of the Donghyun series; no asset of the
  original game is used. The MIT license applies to the Donghyunsim code and
  documentation; the page fonts are under the SIL Open Font License. See
  LICENSE and CREDITS.md.
keywords:
  - city-building game
  - SimCity
  - esoteric programming language
  - JavaScript
